  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on calculating an unweighted average of all outcomes and comparing how many outcomes in each lottery exceed this value. The individual does not mention any such average, threshold, or counting of outcomes above a benchmark. Instead, their reasoning is based on risk and certainty—focusing on the guaranteed win in A versus the chance of zero in B. There is no overlap in the information used (no average computed, no counting of outcomes above a threshold) and no alignment with the rule of the decision reason (comparing counts of outcomes above average). The individual’s justification is based on risk aversion, not a mechanical count of outcomes relative to a mean. Therefore, there is no evidence that the decision reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
